<!-- WHEEL SIZING GUIDE -->
<section class="block" id="fitmentSec"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="sec-head"><div class="sec-eye">Good to know</div><h2>Understanding Wheel Fitment</h2>
    <p style="color:#c3d2e8;font-size:15px">Wheels aren&rsquo;t one-size-fits-all. Here&rsquo;s what determines which wheels fit your vehicle &mdash; and what our wheel search checks automatically.</p></div>
  <div class="sz-grid">
    <div class="sz-card"><div class="sz-img"><img src="{{ 'netlify-wheel-brands-source-08-a3d1491554d40e77.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Wheel bolt pattern explained" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="sz-body"><div><h3>Bolt pattern</h3><p>The number and spacing of the lug holes (e.g., 5&times;114.3). It must match your vehicle exactly or the wheel won&rsquo;t mount. This is the first filter the search applies.</p></div></div></div>
    <div class="sz-card"><div class="sz-img"><img src="{{ 'netlify-wheel-brands-source-09-5ae8bdb2ffda8071.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Wheel offset explained" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="sz-body"><div><h3>Offset &amp; backspacing</h3><p>Offset is how far the mounting surface sits from the wheel&rsquo;s centerline. The wrong offset means the wheel sits too far in (rubbing) or out (sticking past the fender).</p></div></div></div>
    <div class="sz-card"><div class="sz-img"><img src="{{ 'netlify-wheel-brands-source-10-2014f8764e9af53e.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Wheel center bore explained" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="sz-body"><div><h3>Center bore</h3><p>The center hole diameter that fits over the hub. Hub-centric wheels fit precisely; the wrong bore needs adapter rings or won&rsquo;t mount safely.</p></div></div></div>
    <div class="sz-card"><div class="sz-img"><img src="{{ 'netlify-wheel-brands-source-11-b147c4ca0d954f16.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Wheel wheel sizing explained" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="sz-body"><div><h3>Diameter &amp; width</h3><p>Upsizing looks great but affects ride, tire selection, and speedometer accuracy. The search shows what sizes are confirmed safe for your vehicle.</p></div></div></div>
    <div class="sz-card"><div class="sz-img"><img src="{{ 'netlify-wheel-brands-source-12-9ad0fd495855ac63.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Wheel wheel finishes explained" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="sz-body"><div><h3>Finish types</h3><p>Chrome, gloss black, matte, machined, bronze, brushed &mdash; finishes affect appearance and maintenance. Some need special care to avoid peeling or oxidation.</p></div></div></div>
    <div class="sz-card"><div class="sz-img"><img src="{{ 'netlify-wheel-brands-source-13-8dc770f9094e4769.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Wheel load rating explained" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="sz-body"><div><h3>Load rating</h3><p>Every wheel has a weight capacity. Trucks and SUVs need wheels rated for their load &mdash; aftermarket wheels must match or exceed the OE spec.</p></div></div></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

